---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout
  title="CopyPatch v2 documentation"
  description="Embed CopyPatch in your application at the same-origin v2 API route."
>
  <h1>CopyPatch v2</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    CopyPatch adds inline editing to the application you already operate. v2 runs
    inside that application at <code>/__copypatch/api/v2</code>, not in a
    separate server or browser-facing proxy.
  </p>

  <h2>Choose an integration</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Host</th><th>Integration</th><th>Static-only limitation</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Next.js App Router</td><td><code>@copypatch/next</code> route handlers and server snapshot helper</td><td>Use a server route, not static export.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Astro SSR</td><td><code>@copypatch/node</code> native adapter</td><td>Static output can render fallback copy only.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>React Router</td><td><code>@copypatch/node</code> native adapter</td><td>Mount it in the server entry.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Vite + Node</td><td>Native, Express, Fastify, or Hono adapter</td><td>Vite alone does not provide the API runtime.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>What changed from v1</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The v2 API path is <code>/__copypatch/api/v2</code>.</li>
    <li>CopyPatch is mounted in the host application. Do not configure a second port, proxy, or CORS allowlist.</li>
    <li>Choose either SQLite or PostgreSQL persistence.</li>
    <li>Choose the built-in passphrase session or an adapter for the host application's authentication.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Start with <a href="/docs/installation">installation</a>, then choose the
    framework page that matches your application.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
